= The Factory Councils Movement

The factory councils elected under the 1920 law give Communists a foothold in plants where the unions are run by Social Democrats. Councils also run price-control committees as the mark collapses.

- @councils: Build a national congress of factory councils.
- @unions: Work patiently inside the ADGB unions.

@councils
on-arrival: {!
Q.union_influence += 4;
Q.rev_situation += 3;
Q.spd_relation += 2;
Q.right_strength += 2;
!}

Factory council delegates from across the country meet under Communist leadership. The union leaders call it a rival organisation, but SPD members attend.

@unions
on-arrival: {!
Q.union_influence += 7;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.left_dissent += 3;
!}

Communists run for union posts and win some. The Left complains that the party is serving the union bureaucracy instead of fighting it.
